{"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-to-TelemetryDeck","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckSetupError"],"title":"Sending to TelemetryDeck"},{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder"],"title":"Encoding batches"},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckEncodingError"],"title":"Records left out"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},{"text":") for TelemetryDeck in one call. It checks","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the app ID and your organization’s namespace, then posts to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"https:\/\/nom.telemetrydeck.com\/v3\/<namespace>\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder"},{"text":". Each batch is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"split to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"text":": 100 signals a request, as TelemetryDeck’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftSDK sends them; 333,333 bytes a signal, a third of Ingest API v3’s limit of 1,000,000; and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1,000,000 bytes a request, the encoder’s own bound, as TelemetryDeck documents none. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no request. The destination retries no response, a 5xx (TelemetryDeck answers 503 while its queue","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is full), 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. No trace context is sent.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" leaves this module out, so import it on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The app ID only says which app a signal belongs to, and TelemetryDeck’s own SDKs ship it inside"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every app, so the destination builds on every platform and an app sends to TelemetryDeck directly."}]},{"code":["import HTTPDestinations","import TelemetryDeckEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let telemetryDeck = try HTTPDestination.telemetryDeck(","    appID: appID,  \/\/ from the app's settings in the TelemetryDeck dashboard","    namespace: \"com.example\",  \/\/ your organization's namespace","    testMode: false,  \/\/ true for builds whose signals only Test Mode should show","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: telemetryDeck)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The factory throws "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":" for an app ID that is empty or only whitespace,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and for a namespace TelemetryDeck doesn’t take. A namespace holds only ASCII letters, digits, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"."},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":", and can’t be "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"w"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"."},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".."},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"testMode"},{"type":"text","text":" has no default. TelemetryDeck shows test signals only in its Test Mode, apart from your"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"real users, and its SDK picks test mode for debug builds. Pass whatever your app uses to tell its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"builds apart, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#if DEBUG"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" otherwise."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"User-counts-are-sessions","text":"User counts are sessions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TelemetryDeck counts users by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clientUser"},{"type":"text","text":". The destination sends the record’s session, from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sessions enricher, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clientUser"},{"type":"text","text":", hashed the way TelemetryDeck’s SDKs hash a user identifier:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SHA-256 of the lowercase UUID, in lowercase hex, with the SDKs’ default, empty salt."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"TelemetryDeck salts and hashes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clientUser"},{"type":"text","text":" again on its server. The same session is also the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sessionID"},{"type":"text","text":", in the clear, so a salt of the app’s own would hide nothing, and the destination takes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"none. Nothing else identifies a record: no vendor identifier, device identifier or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"account, and no trace context."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"So TelemetryDeck’s user counts are session counts. A person who opens the app three times is three","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"users, and its retention charts show how long a session lasts, not whether people come back. That","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is the library’s default, for privacy. To count devices instead, put","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"StandardContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s ","type":"text"},{"code":"VendorIdentifierKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the records’ context and send them through a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination that reads it, or write your own enricher and encoder that send the identifier you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"choose. This encoder sends the session alone.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record with no session, such as one a store recovered after a relaunch, is its own user: its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clientUser"},{"type":"text","text":" is the hash of the record’s identifier, and it has no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sessionID"},{"type":"text","text":". Making up a session"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"would join unrelated records, and skipping the record would lose it."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"What-TelemetryDeck-receives","text":"What TelemetryDeck receives"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each request is a JSON array of signals, one per record. Every signal has:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appID"},{"type":"text","text":", as given, without surrounding whitespace;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the event’s name;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clientUser"},{"type":"text","text":", the hashed session, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sessionID"},{"type":"text","text":", the session;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"receivedAt"},{"type":"text","text":", the record’s timestamp in ISO 8601 with milliseconds, so a signal sent late still"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"counts at the time it was tracked;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"isTestMode","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"true\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"false\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":";","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"TelemetryDeck.SDK.name","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"text":" the encoder is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"made with, and sit beside these, each keeping its JSON type. TelemetryDeck doesn’t index nested","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values, so an object or array is flattened into dotted names: a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cart"},{"text":" holding ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"size"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cart.size"},{"text":", and the first element of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tags"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tags.0"},{"text":". A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" property is left out. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. No ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"floatValue"},{"text":" is sent.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The standard context, when the record has it, becomes TelemetryDeck’s built-in parameters:"}]},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Context"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parameters"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplicationKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.AppInfo.version"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".buildNumber"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".versionAndBuildNumber"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"TelemetryDeck.Device.modelName","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"OperatingSystemKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"TelemetryDeck.Device.operatingSystem","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".platform","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".systemVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".systemMajorVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":".systemMajorMinorVersion","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.RunContext.locale"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".language"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.UserPreference.region"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The bundle identifier, the form factor and the network aren’t sent.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Records-left-out","text":"Records left out"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name or parameter name, once flattened, holds anything but ASCII letters, digits,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"."},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":", or is empty. TelemetryDeck refuses the whole request for one such name."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name or parameter name starts with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck."},{"type":"text","text":", in any case: TelemetryDeck"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reserves that scope for its SDKs’ parameters and its server’s;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one with a parameter named as one of a signal’s own members, "},{"code":"appID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"clientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"receivedAt","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"type","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"sessionID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"isTestMode","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"floatValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", spelled exactly so: in the flat"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"signal it would replace the member. A name like one in another case, such as "},{"code":"Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", is sent."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose values flatten to the same name twice;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose timestamp falls outside the years 1 to 9999, which TelemetryDeck can’t parse;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose JSON is over 333,333 bytes. TelemetryDeck refuses the whole request for a signal over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1,000,000 bytes as its server writes it, which may be larger than the encoder’s; a third leaves"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"room for the escapes a re-encoder commonly adds."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The destination reports each as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckEncodingError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". When the destination is made, it logs a notice for each event and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property of the plan whose name would be left out."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"What-TelemetryDeck-doesnt-report","text":"What TelemetryDeck doesn’t report"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TelemetryDeck answers 200 to any namespace and any app ID it can read, so a typo in either loses"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every signal without an error. Check that the first signals show up in the dashboard, in Test Mode"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"testMode"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TelemetryDeck doesn’t remove duplicates. A record is sent more than once when a request is retried"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after TelemetryDeck stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a cancelled batch"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again, and when a store redelivers records after a relaunch, and TelemetryDeck counts each copy."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what TelemetryDeck receives, and why, in more detail."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"Send records to TelemetryDeck as signals, through its Ingest API v3.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","externalID":"TelemetryDeckEncoding","modules":[{"name":"TelemetryDeckEncoding"}],"title":"TelemetryDeckEncoding"},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://TelemetryDeckEncoding/documentation/TelemetryDeckEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"telemetryDeck"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"appID"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"namespace"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"testMode"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"plan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","text":"TrackingPlan"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"transport"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"backoff"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","text":"ExponentialBackoff"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"clock"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","text":"Clock"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":">) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:21TelemetryDeckEncoding0aB10SetupErrorO","text":"TelemetryDeckSetupError"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","text":"HTTPDestination"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:21TelemetryDeckEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV","text":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"url":"\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/telemetrydeck(appid:namespace:testmode:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","title":"telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends batches to the TelemetryDeck app "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appID"},{"type":"text","text":", in the organization’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"namespace"},{"type":"text","text":", marking every event as a test event or not as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"testMode"},{"type":"text","text":" says, through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transport"},{"type":"text","text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the waits of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}],"title":"HTTPDestinations"},"doc://TelemetryDeckEncoding/documentation/TelemetryDeckEncoding/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of TelemetryDeck’s Ingest API v3, so an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can send events to an organization’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/v3\/<namespace>\/"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding\/telemetrydeckbatchencoder","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder"},"doc://TelemetryDeckEncoding/documentation/TelemetryDeckEncoding/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding\/telemetrydeckbatchencoder\/batchlimit","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchLimit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchLimit","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV"}],"abstract":[{"text":"TelemetryDeck’s limits on one request: 100 even